WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.851
A pattern rule expresses the starting amount and change using a letter such as n.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:11.139
A rule starts at 12 and increases by 10 per step. Which expression describes it? The

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:16.239
answer is 12 plus 10n. Initial value 12, then add 10 for each step n.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:22.838
A price table in a recycling club starts at 22 and adds 2 for each new step. Which

00:00:22.838 --> 00:00:26.653
expression gives the value at step n? Pause to choose and explain.

00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:33.218
A price table in a recycling club starts at 22 and adds 2 for each new step. Which

00:00:33.218 --> 00:00:38.272
expression gives the value at step n? The answer is 22 plus 2n. Initial value 22,

00:00:38.272 --> 00:00:40.483
then add 2 for each step n.
